---
description: Core instructions for every project file
alwaysApply: true
---
- First inspect the repository, package.json, Astro configuration, existing components, and styling approach before editing.
- Preserve the existing architecture and dependencies unless a change is necessary and explained.
- Prefer simple, maintainable Astro-first solutions. Use server-rendered/static Astro components by default; add client-side JavaScript only for real interaction.
- Do not introduce React, Vue, Svelte, or another UI framework unless the project already uses it or the user explicitly requests it.
- Never invent client facts, testimonials, credentials, statistics, certifications, prices, guarantees, or service claims. Flag missing content with clear placeholders.
- Keep secrets and private client data out of source control. Never place private API keys in browser-side code.
- Before finishing, summarize changes, checks run, checks not run, and any remaining risks.
